## 1. Exact model and physical contract

Let the old qubits be 1,2, the source qubits A,B, and

\[
K=2I+Z_1Z_2,\quad \theta=\arctan(4/3),\quad
j=2\theta/\pi,\quad u=1/2,
\]
\[
g^2=(\pi^2-\theta^2)/(\pi T),\quad
\lambda=(\pi-\theta)/T,\quad
L=(X_AX_B+Y_AY_B)/2.
\]

The installed generator being checked is exactly

\[
H=K+j(I-L)+u|11\rangle\langle11|
 +g(I+X_1X_A)+g(I+X_2X_B)+\lambda I.
\]

The literal old K remains installed. The permitted topology has old edge 1–2, source edge A–B, and ports 1–A and 2–B. Thus this is a degree-two square, provided the specified blocks on its edges are supplied. The new source interaction and simultaneous static XX ports are physical premises. They do not follow from the earlier four onsite rays, an at-most-one-active-port restriction, or microscopic axioms. The source initialization is the independent product state |00>, including independence from an arbitrary correlated old/reference input. It is simpler than a Bell input but is still a supplied initialization and installation interface.

Using the usual Pauli convention, L exchanges |01> and |10>, and annihilates |00> and |11>. In the ordered source eigenbasis |00>, Psi+, Psi−, |11>,

\[
\operatorname{spec}(H_c)=(j,0,2j,j+u).
\]

Since pi/4 < theta < pi/3, we have 1/2 < j < 2/3. Both source terms are positive, and j>u gives ||Hc||=2j. In particular |00> is an excited source eigenstate of energy j, not a zero-energy or ground-state input. Every displayed added block is positive. Positivity of the source block is not a claim that its hopping Pauli summands individually have positive coefficients and spectra; the permitted positive block is j(I−L), or an explicitly justified positive decomposition of that block.

## 2. Full complementary-space gap and an independent invariant block

Put J psi=psi tensor |00>, P=JJ*, Q=I−P, and

\[
H_0=K+H_c-jI=K-jL+u|11\rangle\langle11|,
\qquad V=g(X_1X_A+X_2X_B).
\]

Then H0 J=JK and J*VJ=0. The two port Paulis commute, so ||V||=2g. The old energies are 1 and 3. Relative to the code source eigenvalue zero, the complementary source energies are −j,+j,u. Consequently all full Q-to-P spectral differences, including matrix elements not reached by a first perturbation, are

\[
\{\pm j,\ \pm j\pm2,\ u,\ u\pm2\}.
\]

Their minimum absolute value is exactly 1/2: j>1/2, 2−j>4/3, u=1/2, and 2−u=3/2. This is a full Sylvester gap and does not require a lowest-energy code band or a restriction to initially accessible states.

For a more direct check, choose a unit simultaneous old eigenvector psi of ZZ and XX with eigenvalues z,x in {−1,+1}. Since X2 psi=x X1 psi,

\[
VJ\psi=gX_1\psi\otimes(|10\rangle+x|01\rangle).
\]

The old vector X1 psi has parity −z and the source vector has L eigenvalue x. Define the orthonormal vectors

\[
e_0=\psi|00\rangle,\quad
e_1=X_1\psi(|10\rangle+x|01\rangle)/\sqrt2,\quad
e_2=\psi|11\rangle.
\]

Their span is invariant under H0+V. After subtracting the old energy k=2+z, the exact matrix is

\[
\begin{pmatrix}
0&\sqrt2g&0\\
\sqrt2g&-2z-jx&x\sqrt2g\\
0&x\sqrt2g&u
\end{pmatrix}.
\]

This analytic three-state reduction independently checks the signs, the factor sqrt(2), the second excitation, and the support of the first two correctors. It is not a numerical diagonalization. The full-space gap argument above, rather than this invariant-block restriction alone, justifies the Sylvester inverse on arbitrary right-hand sides.

## 3. Second order and the u=0 stress test

The first corrector obeys H0 S1−S1 K=−VJ and lies in Q. On psi it is

\[
S_1\psi={g\over 2z+jx}\,X_1\psi\otimes(|10\rangle+x|01\rangle).
\]

Applying V again gives

\[
VS_1\psi=h_2(z,x)\,\psi\otimes|00\rangle
 +x h_2(z,x)\,\psi\otimes|11\rangle,
\qquad h_2(z,x)={2g^2\over2z+jx}.
\]

Therefore

\[
H_2=J^*VS_1={2g^2(2ZZ-jXX)\over4-j^2}
 ={\pi ZZ-\theta XX\over T}.
\]

Here the reciprocal identity follows from (2z+jx)(2z−jx)=4−j^2, and substituting j and g gives 2g^2/(4−j^2)=pi/(2T). H2 is Hermitian and commutes with K. There is no sign ambiguity from a negative energy denominator: it was retained explicitly in S1.

The same calculation establishes a precise failed route at u=0. The second corrector would have to solve

\[
(H_0 S_2-S_2K)\psi=-x h_2(z,x)\,\psi|11\rangle.
\]

At u=0 its displayed matrix entry has zero denominator and nonzero numerator for every z,x and g>0. Hence that Sylvester equation has no solution. At u=1/2 it has the explicit solution S2 psi=−x h2(z,x) psi|11>/u. This is a concrete obstruction to the unpenalized *second-corrector proof route*, not a theorem that every u=0 device, different target, or different timing is impossible. In particular it is not a broad no-go submission, and no fictitious collection of failed architectures is supplied.

## 4. Purposeful old scalar and full endpoint phase

The old effective generator is K+H2+lambda I. Its correction has eigenvalues

\[
T(H_2+\lambda I):\quad
2\pi-2\theta,\ 2\pi,\ -2\theta,\ 0
\]

for (z,x)=(+,+),(+,−),(−,+),(−,−), respectively. Thus its norm is 2pi/T. At time T,

\[
e^{-iT(H_2+\lambda I)}
=e^{-i(\pi-\theta)}e^{-i\pi ZZ}e^{i\theta XX}
=e^{i\theta}e^{i\theta XX}=W.
