Indeed cos(theta)=3/5 and sin(theta)=4/5 give the required I coefficient (9+12i)/25 and XX coefficient (−16+12i)/25. Without lambda the phase is e^{i(pi−theta)}W, so removing that scalar would change the full isometry. The positive old identity is a purposeful phase control, not a dropped source reserve.

