The window w=epsilon T/256 is positive and <=T/256, so all relevant t are <2T. Since K and H2+lambda commute, the additional endpoint-to-window drift is bounded by s||H2+lambda||<8w/T=epsilon/32. This yields ||e^(−itH)J−Ct||<3epsilon/32 throughout [T,T+w]. The comparison follows actual old aging e^(−isK), rather than holding the old state fixed.

